started-at: <time>
-----
-----
Code-commandments — when the session's last shell command started, and the changed judged files and their times then.

The block above the first divider is this file's state, one `name: value` per line:
  started-at  unix nanoseconds when the hook was handed the command; a changed file modified since is one it wrote

Between the dividers is the list: a file path, a tab, then its modification time in nanoseconds

Safe to delete — the next shell command's changes are not counted as the session's.

